    "question": {
      ":question/id": "0058268f-5e42-5fd4-b656-2738cb5a8971",
      ":question/problem": "Calculate $X+Y+Z$, where\n\n$$\nX=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix},\\,Y=\\begin{bmatrix}7 & 7 \\\\ -3 & 3\\end{bmatrix},\\,Z=\\begin{bmatrix}-6 & -4 \\\\ -8 & -8\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\n| $X+Y+Z=\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-1}} | {{field-2}} |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-3}} | {{field-4}} |  |  |",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Performing the operations on each corresponding entry, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}X+Y+Z & =\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}7 & 7 \\\\ -3 & 3\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}-6 & -4 \\\\ -8 & -8\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-2+7+(-6) & 1+7+(-4) \\\\ 0+(-3)+(-8) & 2+3+(-8)\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 4 \\\\ -11 & -3\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
